From 9a2a1ad519b4e76df8fe73773edfcb2728716ca4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/encode_video: report a failure to set the preset

The example sets the "preset" private option to "slow" for every
H.264 encoder and ignores the result. Not every H.264 encoder has such
an option (h264_vaapi and h264_v4l2m2m do not), and in that case the
request is dropped without a word.

Print the error returned by av_opt_set() so that the user knows the
option was not applied. It is not treated as fatal, as encoding can
continue with the encoder's defaults.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/encode_video.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/encode_video.c b/doc/examples/encode_video.c
index c8168a1..d429b3c 100644
--- a/doc/examples/encode_video.c
+++ b/doc/examples/encode_video.c
@@ -123,8 +123,11 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
     c->max_b_frames = 1;
     c->pix_fmt = AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P;
 
-    if (codec->id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264)
-        av_opt_set(c->priv_data, "preset", "slow", 0);
+    if (codec->id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264) {
+        ret = av_opt_set(c->priv_data, "preset", "slow", 0);
+        if (ret < 0)
+            fprintf(stderr, "Could not set the preset: %s\n", av_err2str(ret));
+    }
 
     /* open it */
     ret = avcodec_open2(c, codec, NULL);
